        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "$\\cos(C) = \\frac{105}{126}$ (not simplified)"
        }
      ],
      "correctOptionIndex": 0,
      "feedback": {
        "correct": {
          "explanation": "Perfect! $\\cos(C) = \\frac{7^2 + 9^2 - 5^2}{2(7)(9)} = \\frac{49 + 81 - 25}{126} = \\frac{105}{126} = \\frac{5}{6}$ (dividing by GCD 21).",
          "insight": "Positive cosine means $C$ is acute (less than 90°). Makes sense since 5 is the smallest side!"
        },
        "incorrect": {
          "1": "Calculate: $\\frac{49+81-25}{126} = \\frac{105}{126}$. Simplify: divide both by 21 to get $\\frac{5}{6}$.",
          "2": "This is correct but not fully simplified. $\\frac{105}{126} = \\frac{5}{6}$ after dividing by 21."
        }
      },
      "resultState": {
        "description": "Found cos(C) = 5/6"
      }
